{"id":"mahabharata-7-071","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":71,"title":"एकसप्ततितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 71 · Many duels at Drona's array","summary":{"en":"Sanjaya describes the fighting of the Pandava and Kuru warriors in duels, as Shaibya, Shakuni, Nakula and Sahadeva and others clash. The Kaurava princes keep Bhima engaged.","kn":"ಪಾಂಡವ-ಕುರು ವೀರರ ದ್ವಂದ್ವಯುದ್ಧಗಳನ್ನು ಸಂಜಯ ವರ್ಣಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಶೈಬ್ಯ, ಶಕುನಿ, ನಕುಲ-ಸಹದೇವ ಮತ್ತಿತರರು ಹೋರಾಡುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಕೌರವ ರಾಜಕುಮಾರರು ಭೀಮನನ್ನು ತೊಡಗಿಸಿಕೊಳ್ಳುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"संजय पाण्डव और कुरु वीरों के द्वन्द्वयुद्धों का वर्णन करते हैं, जिनमें शैब्य, शकुनि, नकुल-सहदेव आदि भिड़ते हैं। कौरव राजकुमार भीम को उलझाए रखते हैं।","te":"పాండవ కురు వీరుల ద్వంద్వయుద్ధాలను సంజయుడు వర్ణిస్తాడు; శైబ్యుడు, శకుని, నకుల సహదేవులు ఇతరులు తలపడతారు. కౌరవ రాకుమారులు భీముని నిమగ్నం చేస్తారు.","ta":"பாண்டவ குரு வீரர்களின் தனிப்போர்களைச் சஞ்சயன் விவரிக்கிறான்; சைப்யன், சகுனி, நகுலன் சகதேவன் முதலியோர் மோதுகின்றனர். கௌரவ இளவரசர் பீமனைப் போரில் ஈடுபடுத்துகின்றனர்.","ml":"പാണ്ഡവ, കുരു വീരന്മാരുടെ മെയ്പ്പോര് ദ്വന്ദ്വയുദ്ധങ്ങളായി സഞ്ജയൻ വിവരിക്കുന്നു; ശൈബ്യനും ശകുനിയും നകുലനും സഹദേവനും മറ്റുള്ളവരും ഏറ്റുമുട്ടുന്നു. കൗരവ രാജകുമാരന്മാർ ഭീമനെ പിടിച്ചുനിർത്തുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.71; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"जयद्रथवधपर्व","titleEn":"Jayadrathavadha Parva (Slaying of Jayadratha)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"राजन्संग्राममाश्चर्यं शृणु कीर्तयतो मम ।\nकुरूणां पाण्डवानां च यथा युद्धमवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, listen as I tell of the wondrous battle, how the fighting went between the Kurus and the Pandavas."}},{"n":2,"text":"भारद्वाजं समासाद्य व्यूहस्य प्रमुखे स्थितम् ।\nअयोधयन्रणे पार्था द्रोणानीकं बिभित्सवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Bharadvaja's son, who stood at the front of the formation, the Pandavas fought in the battle, wishing to break Drona's division."}},{"n":3,"text":"रक्षमाणाः स्वकं व्यूहं द्रोणस्यापि च सैनिकाः ।\nअयोधयन्रणे पार्थान्प्रार्थयन्तो महद्यशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona's soldiers too, guarding their own formation and seeking great fame, fought the Pandavas in the battle."}},{"n":4,"text":"विन्दानुविन्दावावन्त्यौ विराटं दशभिः शरैः ।\nआजघ्नतुः सुसंक्रुद्धौ तव पुत्रहितैषिणौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Avantis Vinda and Anuvinda, in great wrath, wishing well to your sons, struck Virata with ten arrows."}},{"n":5,"text":"विराटश्च महाराज तावुभौ समरे स्थितौ ।\nपराक्रान्तौ पराक्रम्य योधयामास सानुगौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"And Virata, great king, standing against them both in battle, showed his valour and fought those two valiant men with their followers."}},{"n":6,"text":"तेषां युद्धं समभवद्दारुणं शोणितोदकम् ।\nसिंहस्य द्विपमुख्याभ्यां प्रभिन्नाभ्यां यथा वने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their battle was dreadful, with water that was blood, like the fight of a lion against two rutting chief elephants in a forest."}},{"n":7,"text":"बाह्लीकं रभसं युद्धे याज्ञसेनिर्महाबलः ।\nआजघ्ने विशिखैस्तीक्ष्णैर्घोरैर्मर्मास्थिभेदिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty son of Yajnasena struck the impetuous Bahlika in the battle with sharp, terrible arrows that break vital parts and bones."}},{"n":8,"text":"बाह्लीको याज्ञसेनिं तु हेमपुङ्खैः शिलाशितैः ।\nआजघान भृशं क्रुद्धो नवभिर्नतपर्वभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bahlika, greatly enraged, struck Yajnasena's son with nine stone-sharpened, gold-feathered, smooth-jointed arrows."}},{"n":9,"text":"तद्युद्धमभवद्घोरं शरशक्तिसमाकुलम् ।\nभीरूणां त्रासजननं शूराणां हर्षवर्धनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That battle was terrible, crowded with arrows and spears, bringing fear to the timid and joy to the brave."}},{"n":10,"text":"ताभ्यां तत्र शरैर्मुक्तैरन्तरिक्षं दिशस्तथा ।\nअभवत्संवृतं सर्वं न प्राज्ञायत किंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the arrows loosed there by the two, the sky and the quarters were covered; nothing could be made out."}},{"n":11,"text":"शैब्यो गोवासनो युद्धे काश्यपुत्रं महारथम् ।\nससैन्यो योधयामास गजः प्रतिगजं यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gobasana the Shaibya, with his army, fought the Kashi prince, the great chariot-warrior, in the battle, like an elephant against an elephant."}},{"n":12,"text":"बाह्लीकराजः संरब्धो द्रौपदेयान्महारथान् ।\nमनः पञ्चेन्द्रियाणीव शुशुभे योधयन्रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king of the Bahlikas, in fury, shone as he fought the great chariot-warrior sons of Draupadi, like the mind fighting the five senses."}},{"n":13,"text":"अयोधयंस्ते च भृशं तं शरौघैः समन्ततः ।\nइन्द्रियार्था यथा देहं शश्वद्देहभृतां वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"They fought him fiercely on all sides with floods of arrows, as the objects of the senses always press on the body, best of embodied beings."}},{"n":14,"text":"वार्ष्णेयं सात्यकिं युद्धे पुत्रो दुःशासनस्तव ।\nआजघ्ने सायकैस्तीक्ष्णैर्नवभिर्नतपर्वभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your son Duhshasana struck the Vrishni Satyaki in the battle with nine sharp, smooth-jointed arrows."}},{"n":15,"text":"सोऽतिविद्धो बलवता महेष्वासेन धन्विना ।\nईषन्मूर्छां जगामाशु सात्यकिः सत्यविक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Deeply wounded by that strong and mighty archer, Satyaki of true valour quickly swooned a little."}},{"n":16,"text":"समाश्वस्तस्तु वार्ष्णेयस्तव पुत्रं महारथम् ।\nविव्याध दशभिस्तूर्णं सायकैः कङ्कपत्रिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Recovering, the Vrishni quickly pierced your son, the great chariot-warrior, with ten heron-feathered arrows."}},{"n":17,"text":"तावन्योन्यं दृढं विद्धावन्योन्यशरविक्षतौ ।\nरेजतुः समरे राजन्पुष्पिताविव किंशुकौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those two, deeply pierced and wounded by each other's arrows, shone in the battle, O king, like two kimshuka trees in flower."}},{"n":18,"text":"अलम्बुसस्तु संक्रुद्धः कुन्तिभोजशरार्दितः ।\nअशोभत परं लक्ष्म्या पुष्पाढ्य इव किंशुकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Alambusa, in great wrath, afflicted by Kuntibhoja's arrows, shone greatly with splendour, like a kimshuka rich in blossoms."}},{"n":19,"text":"कुन्तिभोजं ततो रक्षो विद्ध्वा बहुभिरायसैः ।\nअनदद्भैरवं नादं वाहिन्याः प्रमुखे तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"The rakshasa, after piercing Kuntibhoja with many iron arrows, gave a terrible roar at the front of your army."}},{"n":20,"text":"ततस्तौ समरे शूरौ योधयन्तौ परस्परम् ।\nददृशुः सर्वभूतानि शक्रजम्भौ यथा पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"All beings watched those two heroes fighting each other in the battle, as they once watched Shakra and Jambha."}},{"n":21,"text":"शकुनिं रभसं युद्धे कृतवैरं च भारत ।\nमाद्रीपुत्रौ च संरब्धौ शरैरर्दयतां मृधे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shakuni, impetuous in the battle and long hostile, was harassed with arrows in the fight by the two sons of Madri, enraged."}},{"n":22,"text":"तन्मूलः स महाराज प्रावर्तत जनक्षयः ।\nत्वया संजनितोऽत्यर्थं कर्णेन च विवर्धितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"O great king, the slaughter of men began with him as its root; you brought it about, Karna increased it,"}},{"n":23,"text":"उद्धुक्षितश्च पुत्रेण तव क्रोधहुताशनः ।\nय इमां पृथिवीं राजन्दग्धुं सर्वां समुद्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"and your son fanned the fire of wrath that is now ready to burn this whole earth."}},{"n":24,"text":"शकुनिः पाण्डुपुत्राभ्यां कृतः स विमुखः शरैः ।\nनाभ्यजानत कर्तव्यं युधि किंचित्पराक्रमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shakuni was turned away by arrows from the two sons of Pandu, and in the battle did not know what valour he should show."}},{"n":25,"text":"विमुखं चैनमालोक्य माद्रीपुत्रौ महारथौ ।\nववर्षतुः पुनर्बाणैर्यथा मेघौ महागिरिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him turned away, the two great chariot-warriors, sons of Madri, again poured arrows on him like two clouds on a great mountain."}},{"n":26,"text":"स वध्यमानो बहुभिः शरैः संनतपर्वभिः ।\nसंप्रायाज्जवनैरश्वैर्द्रोणानीकाय सौबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by many smooth-jointed arrows, the son of Subala went off with his swift horses to Drona's division."}},{"n":27,"text":"घटोत्कचस्तथा शूरं राक्षसं तमलायुधम् ।\nअभ्ययाद्रभसं युद्धे वेगमास्थाय मध्यमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ghatotkacha then advanced in the battle against the brave rakshasa Alayudha, taking a middle speed."}},{"n":28,"text":"तयोर्युद्धं महाराज चित्ररूपमिवाभवत् ।\nयादृशं हि पुरा वृत्तं रामरावणयोर्मृधे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their fight, great king, was like a painting, such as took place of old in the battle of Rama and Ravana."}},{"n":29,"text":"ततो युधिष्ठिरो राजा मद्रराजानमाहवे ।\nविद्ध्वा पञ्चाशता बाणैः पुनर्विव्याध सप्तभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Yudhishthira in the battle pierced the king of the Madras with fifty arrows and again with seven."}},{"n":30,"text":"ततः प्रववृते युद्धं तयोरत्यद्भुतं नृप ।\nयथा पूर्वं महद्युद्धं शम्बरामरराजयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O king, a most wondrous battle started between those two, like the great battle once between Shambara and the king of the gods."}},{"n":31,"text":"विविंशतिश्चित्रसेनो विकर्णश्च तवात्मजः ।\nअयोधयन्भीमसेनं महत्या सेनया वृताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vivimshati, Chitrasena and your son Vikarna, surrounded by a great army, fought Bhimasena."}}]}]}